Great idea!
You could also be hit by some of your items that fall down when you suddenly
are too small to hold them.

More suggestions:
Applying a leash that is already in use.  An evil player (chaotic) might
enjoy to tie his cat to his dog and watch them stumble around.
A more practical use would be to tie the dog to some heavy object (or a
door knob) so it don't eat all the monsters you want to take to the altar.
You could also tie an unused leash (or iron chain) to an item and drag it out of 
a shop.  There could be some chance that the shopkeeper grabs a weapon and cuts 
the leash. If he don't succeed, he'll call the kops as usual.

Making traps.  It is already possible to make pits and trapdoors.
One could set up a dart trap, or a trap with more powerful weapons. (A great
way to get rid of those weapons the monsters leave.)  
A sleep trap could be set up with a wand of sleep or some potions of paralysis.
Ideally, all dangerous potions or wands could be used for making traps.
There could be some limitations to this.  It takes some intelligence to 
make a good trap. (i.e. one that the monsters don't see immediately)
It should be possible to put a potion on top of a door, then wait for a
monster to walk through.  It would have the same effect as throwing the potion,
except that you don't need to be there.
